# Implementation Plan - Phase 3 Debate & Phase 4 Shadow Sandbox Redesign (`ImplementationSD.md`)

Execute a comprehensive multi-phase redesign of the Phase 3 Debate Engine and Phase 4 Shadow Sandbox as outlined in [`ImplementationSD.md`](file:///c:/Users/Shashank/OneDrive/Desktop/Smart%20horizon%20hackathon/ImplementationSD.md). 

This refactoring replaces fragile string-based shell/SQL heuristics with a **versioned typed remediation intent contract (`autosre.action.proposed.v2`)**, a **declarative capability registry**, **fail-closed policy enforcement**, **shadow attestation**, an **explicit state machine harness**, and a **statistically calibrated confidence model**.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Architectural Changes & Security Model**
> 1. **Typed Remediation Intent Contract (`autosre.action.proposed.v2`)**: Phase 3 will no longer output free-form shell strings or arbitrary raw SQL. Instead, it will output typed, schema-validated remediation intents.
> 2. **Removal of Autonomous Raw Shell/SQL Execution**: `execute_sql_command` and `execute_shell_command` fallback paths will be removed from autonomous execution. All actions must resolve to registered, parameterized capabilities.
> 3. **Fail-Closed Policy Enforcement**: Unknown targets, tools, or policy combinations will fail closed with explicit reason codes (`BLOCKED_UNKNOWN_CAPABILITY`, `BLOCKED_TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `BLOCKED_POLICY`) instead of passing through or falling back to generic `api-gateway`.
> 4. **Calibrated Confidence**: Low confidence will no longer be artificially driven by static target/tool penalties (e.g. 0.64 cap for Postgres/`run_query`). Execution confidence will use Beta-binomial historical smoothing, uncertainty metrics, and distinct diagnosis vs mapping vs execution scores.

